body:
@acli I had no idea of plain-text viewer.
But I disagree with you. In your rhetoric, `<a>` doesn't make sense too.

The purpose of `<q>` is its contents are somebody's words quoted by the author of the document, so as `<rt>` is the ruby annotation of the text before. The quotation mark or parenthesis are just the visual indication and doesn't convey any meanings. Also, you can insert gibberish in `<rp>` which will bother text browser users. Those simple yet pesky tasks should be the job for browsers, which interprets HTML and display it to be comprehensive to humans.
